  "worked_solution": "The set $S$ contains all natural numbers less than or equal to $10.$\n\nTherefore, the set can be written as\n\n$$\nS={x\\in N\\,:\\,x\\le 10}.\n$$\n\n**Note**: This definition is not unique. For example:\n\n- We can write $x\\in Z.$ This gives\n\n$$\nS={x\\in Z\\,:1\\le x\\le 10}.\n$$\n\n- We can write $x<11.$ This gives\n\n$$\nS={x\\in N\\,:\\,x<11},\n$$\n\nor, writing $x\\in Z$ as before, we have\n\n$$\nS={x\\in Z\\,:\\,0<x<11}.\n$$",
